Only partially eaten for food items (including corpses) has been 
implemented. So if a wax (or tallow) candle doesn't grow lighter while 
it burns then why should the candelabra.

I only addressed the omission of candle weight from the candelabra and 
didn't open the can (of worms) of aged, damaged or partially used items.

Actually the DevTeam has opeened that can as they have addressed the 
partially eaten food items.

To code the rest could follow these steps:

1. Adjust weight for lightable items based on turns left. (in weight())

2. Make a case structure based on items material and handle the two 
erode flags. (in weight()) As rusted wands would be heavier the rusting 
of wands would affect the game.

3. Remove inventory weight adjustment from various places in the code 
and add it into the main moveloop after the check of the hero's movement 
and after all monsters have moved (check both PC and monster inventories 
on the current level). This ensures that all weight adjustments are 
taken into account after the time consuming action is done.

